# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  rtos-manager commit message template  (git config --local commit.template .gitmessage)
#
#  Every line starting with '#' is stripped by git; the message that gets
#  recorded is what is left. Keep the subject line as the first non-comment
#  line: <type>(<scope>): <subject>, imperative, lower-case, no trailing period,
#  72 characters at most, blank line before any body.
#
#  <type>   feat      a new feature                     -> Added
#           fix       a bug fix                          -> Fixed
#           docs      documentation only                 -> Documentation
#           style     formatting, no code change         -> skipped in CHANGELOG
#           refactor  neither feature nor fix            -> Changed
#           perf      performance improvement            -> Performance
#           test      tests only                         -> Testing
#           build     build system / dependencies        -> Build
#           ci        CI or tooling configuration        -> skipped in CHANGELOG
#           chore     maintenance (release commits)      -> skipped in CHANGELOG
#           revert    revert a previous commit           -> Reverted
#
#  <scope>  the module touched: http, config, cli, version, logging, build,
#           docs, release, ... Omit it only for repo-wide changes.
#
#  Body     *why* the change is needed, in plain prose, wrapped at 72 columns.
#           Bullet lists start with "- ". Reference issues as (#123).
#
#  Footer   BREAKING CHANGE: <what breaks and what to do instead>   -> major bump
#           Refs: #123
#           Co-authored-by: Name <email>
#
#  Examples
#    feat(http): add GET /healthz endpoint
#    fix(build): guard git describe when no tags exist
#    refactor(cli)!: return CommandLine by value instead of filling an out-param
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
